## Gotchas (read before debugging)

- **Only 5 pages came out** → that is the Community Edition limit, not a bug
  (`ConversionResult.PdfPageCountBeforeLimit` says how many the content had). The full `SelectPdf.Universal`
  package removes it with the same code.
- **Classic code does not compile** → it uses `using SelectPdf;`, `System.Drawing` types or WebKit/Blink
  settings. See [`migrating-from-classic.md`](https://github.com/selectpdf/ai-tools/blob/main/plugins/selectpdf/skills/selectpdf-lib-htmltopdf-universal-net/reference/migrating-from-classic.md).
- **`HtmlToImage`, `PdfStandard.PdfA1A` / `PdfA2A` / `PdfA3A`, `TableOfContents`, `CreateFormFields`, partial
  conversion or open actions are missing** → those are in the full `SelectPdf.Universal` package only.
- **`MinPageLoadTime` / `MaxPageLoadTime`** still compile but are obsolete: use `ConversionDelay` and
  `NavigationTimeout`.
- **Engine not found on Linux or macOS** → the native package for that runtime is missing, or it does not
  match the process architecture. On Alpine / musl, use the remote engine instead.
- **Boxes or wrong glyphs on Linux** → the host has no fonts for that script. Add `SelectPdf.Universal.Fonts`
  or load web fonts.
- **Page needs WebGL** → WebGL is off by default; set `Options.WebGlEnabled = true`.

